Cell["\<\
Use a complex energy z = energy + I eta with eta > 0 for retarded boundary \
conditions.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->575760533,ExpressionUUID->"c51f7d8e-cf30-b342-82ec-6d16225a8958"],

Cell["\<\
h0 is the onsite block; h1 couples neighboring principal layers. The optional \
upper block defaults to ConjugateTranspose[h1].\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->588408471,ExpressionUUID->"2ceac29b-a9cf-4a4b-955b-9a4707f54b6d"],

Cell["\<\
The current implementation requires an explicit mode: 1 uses iterative \
decimation; 2 and 3 use transfer matrices; 4 and 5 regularize the hopping by \
singular value decomposition.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1296508932,ExpressionUUID->"b0dbfdd7-e5eb-6a4e-8537-06ee3e7186c9"],

Cell["\<\
Modes 2 and 4 invert a hopping block. Modes 3 and 5 use a generalized \
eigenproblem. The option \"\[Delta]SVD\" defaults to 1.*^-7 and affects modes \
4 and 5.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1446215079,ExpressionUUID->"70d833ff-ecab-404f-9147-fec01ac9d3a3"]
}, Closed]],

